        id: 34,
        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "Defendant wanted to break into an office building at night to steal computer servers[cite: 44]. Defendant walked into the building during normal afternoon business hours when the front lobby was open to the public, walked up to the third floor, and hid inside a carpeted janitorial supply closet[cite: 44]. Defendant remained inside the closet until 11:00 PM, well after the building had closed to the public and all security doors had been locked for the night[cite: 44]. At 11:00 PM, Defendant pushed open the closed, unlatched door of the supply closet, stepped out into the darkened third-floor hallway, and walked toward the server room[cite: 44]. However, before Defendant could reach the server room, an armed night security guard rounding the corner spotted Defendant's flashlight and detained him at gunpoint[cite: 44]. The jurisdiction adheres to traditional common law criminal definitions[cite: 44].",
